# PreBoard Exam Checker Mobile App

Android app for importing question banks, generating pre-board exam sets, exporting printable PDFs, scanning answer sheets, and viewing records.

## Project Structure

- `app/` - Android application source code.
- `app/src/main/java/com/pbec/preboardexamchecker/` - Kotlin source files.
- `app/src/main/assets/katex/` - KaTeX assets used for math rendering.
- `reference/` - Scanner/reference images.
- `tools/` - Scanner calibration and validation scripts.
- `INSTRUCTIONS.md` - Official exam blueprint tables.
- `RUN.md` - Quick device install/run commands.

## Build

Run from this `mobile-app` directory:

```bash
./gradlew :app:compileDebugKotlin
./gradlew :app:assembleDebug
```

Install and launch on a connected device:

```bash
./gradlew clean :app:installDebug
adb shell monkey -p com.pbec.preboardexamchecker 1
```

Use a device id when multiple devices are connected:

```bash
adb -s <device-id> shell monkey -p com.pbec.preboardexamchecker 1
```

## Exam Generation

Generated exams include two sets:

- Set A and Set B contain the same selected questions.
- Set A and Set B store separate shuffled question-id orders.
- Exporting or viewing a set uses that set's stored order.

## PDF Export Notes

Question PDF export is optimized for less paper usage:

- Compact 10pt body text.
- Reduced spacing and page margins.
- Question blocks request keep-together layout so choices do not split from the prompt when the block fits on a new page.
- Subject header, `Instruction:`, and `Multiple Choice` are bold.
- `Multiple Choice` is not italic.

Math rendering support:

- Preserves Unicode math symbols where font support exists.
- Uses available fallback fonts such as Noto Math, Noto Symbols, STIX, and symbol fonts.
- Supports superscript/subscript text and `^` / `_` notation in exported PDFs.
- `.xlsx` imports preserve rich-text superscript/subscript formatting for question text and options.

## Useful Checks

```bash
./gradlew :app:compileDebugKotlin
```

This is the fastest local check after Kotlin source changes.
